From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 10:39:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] AndorSolis: fix syntax, model check, gain range and
 single-mode frames in #144

Pull request #144 fixes several problems with older Andor cameras: the
EM gain range is read before the sensor has cooled, the gain range check
accepts only the two endpoints of the range, GetKeepCleanTime raises on
some models, and SetIsolatedCropModeEx is called on cameras that only
implement SetIsolatedCropMode. This commit corrects four defects in that
pull request and removes the parts that are being split out:

- A print in setup_acquisition nested the string's own quote character
  inside an f-string, which is a syntax error before Python 3.12, so the
  module could not be imported on Python 3.11. The quotes now differ.
- The camera model was compared with 'IXION ULTRA' and 'IXON ULTRA', but
  camera_type.get_type returns member names such as 'IXONULTRA', so the
  iXon Ultra never took the SetIsolatedCropModeEx branch and lost the
  crop offsets. Both branches now test 'IXONULTRA' in self.model.
- The EM gain range check used strict comparisons and rejected the
  endpoints of the range. It is now inclusive.
- Single acquisition mode appended downloaded[0] to the image list; it
  now extends the list with the downloaded frames, as the kinetic series
  and fast kinetics branches do.
- The debug prints of the EM gain range and of the attribute dictionary
  are removed.

The fast acquisition setup, the acquisition-start semaphore and the
matching change to the IMAQdx worker are left for a separate pull
request, as the author offered. Without them the single-mode fix is the
only change to the Andor worker and the IMAQdx worker is unchanged.

Verified by byte-compiling the changed files on Python 3.11 and 3.14,
where the original branch fails on 3.11 with the f-string error, and by
importing the module on Python 3.14; the import reaches the Andor DLL
load, which is the first step that cannot run without the SDK.

